Q4: No Dark Time Active Hold Standards (COPC 2.1, 2.2, 4.1)
Criteria / Options: Met
Guidelines & Notes: Sets bounded time window (e.g., '1-2 minutes') with clear diagnostic purpose; refreshes within 90s; returns with gratitude. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
Criteria / Options: Not Met
Guidelines & Notes: Unannounced hold or dead air >2 mins; vague phrasing ('one second'); exceeding refresh ceiling without check-in. Remediation: Active hold timer coaching. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
No Dark Time Active Hold Comments/Notes
Guidelines & Notes: Must be specific and include exact reasons, timestamps, and interaction details why the SA received the score. Required if Not Met.
Q5: Root Cause Resolution (OMG Signal 01 & Recap 2.1)
Criteria / Options: Met
Guidelines & Notes: Systematically isolates variables with structured probing; fixes the core breakdown and verifies proper functionality. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
Criteria / Options: Not Met
Guidelines & Notes: Applies superficial patches; fails to isolate technical variables; leaves core issue unresolved or guesses blindly. Remediation: Diagnostic flowcharts review. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
Root Cause Resolution Comments/Notes
Guidelines & Notes: Must be specific and include exact reasons, timestamps, and interaction details why the SA received the score. Required if Not Met.
Q6: Recap & Escalation Transparency (Recap 2.2, 3.1, 3.2)
Criteria / Options: Met
Guidelines & Notes: Itemizes actions taken; provides ticket ID (#XXXXXXXX); sets realistic 24-48h SLA; confirms recipient email. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
Criteria / Options: Not Met
Guidelines & Notes: Leaves next steps ambiguous; provides no ticket ID or timeline; promises unverified rush turnarounds; no email check. Remediation: Mandatory ticket macro injection. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
Recap & Escalation Transparency Comments/Notes
Guidelines & Notes: Must be specific and include exact reasons, timestamps, and interaction details why the SA received the score. Required if Not Met.
Q7: End-to-End Ownership & Closure (OMG 01, Handshake CC-05, Recap 4.2)
Criteria / Options: Met
Guidelines & Notes: Confirms clear next-step ownership; obtains explicit affirmative close; maintains strict survey integrity. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
Criteria / Options: Not Met
Guidelines & Notes: Deflects responsibility; closes without explicit confirmation ('Have we covered everything?'); begs for 5-star CSAT. Remediation: Pre-closure sequence roleplay. See "OMG QA Rubric v2"
End-to-End Ownership & Closure Comments/Notes
Guidelines & Notes: Must be specific and include exact reasons, timestamps, and interaction details why the SA received the score. Required if Not Met.
