Sheet: OMG QA Rubric v2
Q#: Q1
Signal & Dimension: Goal Alignment & Inquiry Framing (OMG Signal 02 & Handshake CC-02)
Core Evaluation Standard: Restate merchant's core inquiry and intended outcome upfront ("To ensure we are aligned, your goal is to...") to avoid misdirected effort.
Not Met Criteria: Proceeding on assumptions; addressing secondary symptoms while missing core need; failing to ask clarifying alignment questions.
Met Criteria: Restates core inquiry in advisor's own words, confirms desired end state, and secures merchant validation before opening diagnostic tools.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Roleplay 3-sentence goal alignment protocol; practice summarizing complex multi-issue inquiries; calibrate upfront listening skills.
Q#: Q2
Signal & Dimension: Genuine Empathy (OMG Signal 03 & Handshake CC-01)
Core Evaluation Standard: Acknowledge the merchant's situation with authentic, human empathy; validate business impact before technical steps.
Not Met Criteria: Uses canned, robotic boilerplate scripts; brushes past frustration or financial urgency; lacks human warmth.
Met Criteria: Validates the emotional reality and business stakes directly; pairs genuine warmth with immediate, purposeful action.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Practice 'Validate First, Solve Second' coaching drill; roleplay high-urgency merchant scenarios to build authentic tone.
Q#: Q3
Signal & Dimension: Lower Merchant Effort (OMG Signal 02 & Handshake BC-01)
Core Evaluation Standard: Eliminate cognitive friction; review internal logs and ticket history before asking questions; prevent repetition.
Not Met Criteria: Forces merchant to repeat info already provided in chat/history; shifts manual troubleshooting burden onto user.
Met Criteria: Audits admin timeline, tickets, and logs prior to inquiry; executes actions directly on merchant's behalf.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Implement 'Check 3 Systems Before Asking' protocol (Admin, History, Payouts); audit system look-up efficiency.
Q#: Q4
Signal & Dimension: No Dark Time Active Hold Standards (COPC 2.1, 2.2, 4.1)
Core Evaluation Standard: State definite hold boundaries with diagnostic transparency; refresh within 90–120s; avoid unannounced dead air.
Not Met Criteria: Unannounced hold or dead air >2 mins; vague phrasing ('one second'); exceeding refresh ceiling without check-in.
Met Criteria: Sets bounded time window (e.g., '1-2 minutes') with clear diagnostic purpose; refreshes within 90s; returns with gratitude.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Active hold timer coaching; eliminate vague phrasing; drill 'Gratitude over Apology' re-entry scripting.
Q#: Q5
Signal & Dimension: Root Cause Resolution (OMG Signal 01 & Recap 2.1)
Core Evaluation Standard: Diagnose and resolve the underlying root cause through high-yield probing rather than applying temporary surface fixes.
Not Met Criteria: Applies superficial patches; fails to isolate technical variables; leaves core issue unresolved or guesses blindly.
Met Criteria: Systematically isolates variables with structured probing; fixes the core breakdown and verifies proper functionality.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Review technical diagnostic flowcharts; coach on high-yield question stems; practice isolating admin vs theme variables.
Q#: Q6
Signal & Dimension: Recap & Escalation Transparency (Recap 2.2, 3.1, 3.2)
Core Evaluation Standard: Clearly frame action plan, provide reference ticket ID, communicate realistic SLAs, and verify contact email.
Not Met Criteria: Leaves next steps ambiguous; provides no ticket ID or timeline; promises unverified rush turnarounds; no email check.
Met Criteria: Itemizes actions taken; provides ticket ID (#XXXXXXXX); sets realistic 24-48h SLA; confirms recipient email.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Escalation logging calibration; enforce mandatory ticket macro injection and verified email confirmation.
Q#: Q7
Signal & Dimension: End-to-End Ownership & Closure (OMG 01, Handshake CC-05, Recap 4.2)
Core Evaluation Standard: Take complete ownership of the path forward; secure affirmative pre-closure confirmation; zero survey manipulation.
Not Met Criteria: Deflects responsibility; closes without explicit confirmation ('Have we covered everything?'); begs for 5-star CSAT.
Met Criteria: Confirms clear next-step ownership; obtains explicit affirmative close; maintains strict survey integrity.
Evaluation Score: 
Remediation Protocol: Roleplay 'Who Owns What' handoff; enforce pre-closure confirmation sequence; mandatory review of survey integrity policy.
